  "body": "Research only. No code comes from this issue (AGENTS.md \"needs-research\").\n\n**Why.** Many hobby router owners (WorkBee, Shapeoko, X-Carve, Onefinity, Laguna and Grizzly routers) use Vectric's **VCarve** or Delft Spline's **DeskProto**. Both are known for getting a first part cut quickly. One such user, MisterMaker on Discord (WorkBee with an Estlcam controller, #3038), never uses 3D CAM because building a 3D part from a 2D sketch is \"too much of a hassle\". Asked by the user (mkinney), 2026-11-20.\n\n**Clean-room boundary** (same as #3045). The vendors' public material (feature pages, published manuals and tutorials, public videos) is used only as a checklist of which workflows and features hobby users expect. Never copied: wording, UI labels, parameter names, screen layouts, icons or dialog flows. Behaviour is specced from machining knowledge and our own design.\n\n**Open questions**\n1. **Typical first job.** What steps does a typical hobby job take in each tool: job and material setup, importing a 2D or 3D source, choosing toolpaths, the tool database, preview, saving G-code? Where does CamCraft take more steps or more knowledge today? Compare on 3 to 5 typical jobs: a sign, a V-carved name, an inlay, a 3D relief from an STL or image, a pocket and profile with tabs.\n2. **Missing features.** Which hobby-router features do we lack or only half-cover? Candidates: V-carving (#1443), inlays, text and fonts, relief from an image or heightmap, tabs and bridges, ramps and lead-ins, \"cut out\" profiling, nesting (see #2395), toolpath templates, simple job wizards, machine and post pickers for common routers, simulated preview in wood colours.\n3. **Defaults and presets.** Which defaults and starter presets would let a new router user get a safe first cut with no CAM knowledge? Router tool libraries (end mills, V-bits, ball noses) with conservative feeds, machine presets, material thickness and zero-point prompts.\n4. **What not to copy.** Which of their simplifications would break our \"never gouge, refuse with a reason\" rules, and how do we keep the safety and still stay simple?\n5. **Priorities.** A ranked list of sub-issues by how many router users each helps.\n\n**Done means:** the questions answered in comments here and the sub-issues filed. Each sub-issue gets one P*, one effort:*, area:*, source:agent, a \"Done means\" line and \"Part of #this\". They are linked back, `needs-research` is dropped and this issue is closed.\n\nRelated: #3045 (conversational and no-model operations, the DXF/DWG route), #1443 (V-carve), #2395 (router tab), #1907 (Laguna and Grizzly routers), #3038 (WorkBee), #1880 (SVG import).\n",
